1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:01,070
Hi.

2
00:00:01,250 --> 00:00:04,430
Thank you so much for taking this course.

3
00:00:04,430 --> 00:00:08,210
I hope it was useful and beneficial for you.

4
00:00:08,540 --> 00:00:13,670
So if you completed the course, you probably have taken the test.

5
00:00:13,850 --> 00:00:17,560
The test consists of 30 questions.

6
00:00:17,570 --> 00:00:22,220
If you scored 20 and more points, congratulations.

7
00:00:22,220 --> 00:00:24,080
You did well on the course.

8
00:00:24,230 --> 00:00:31,820
If you have scored less than 20 points, I would recommend you to refresh your memory and review some

9
00:00:31,820 --> 00:00:36,840
of the lessons and videos and redo some exercises.

10
00:00:37,630 --> 00:00:44,710
So also, I would like to give you some tips on how to continue improving your English skills.

11
00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:53,290
First of all, Google in English, find information, articles, tutorials in English, and have a lot

12
00:00:53,290 --> 00:00:54,700
of reading practice.

13
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:58,520
Second, watch YouTube in English.

14
00:00:58,540 --> 00:01:06,940
There are so many interesting channels related to programming technologies, and you have so many choices

15
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:07,800
what to watch.

16
00:01:07,810 --> 00:01:12,220
And in that way you're going to improve your listening skills.

17
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:16,630
Next, don't be afraid to make mistakes.

18
00:01:16,810 --> 00:01:23,140
No one is perfect, and what matters is progress, not perfection.

19
00:01:23,920 --> 00:01:27,640
Next tip set smart goals.

20
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:35,650
These type of goals are well-defined, time specific, measurable, and achievable.

21
00:01:36,010 --> 00:01:45,080
For example, you can set a goal like I want to be able to read technical documentation in English in

22
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:46,150
three weeks.

23
00:01:46,160 --> 00:01:48,650
That would be an example of a smart goal.

24
00:01:48,860 --> 00:01:55,730
Or by the end of this month, I want to learn 15 English idioms.

25
00:01:56,090 --> 00:01:57,200
That is also a smart.

26
00:01:58,310 --> 00:01:59,190
Next thing.

27
00:01:59,210 --> 00:02:00,590
Reward yourself.

28
00:02:00,890 --> 00:02:03,950
So after achieving a goal.

29
00:02:04,790 --> 00:02:06,320
Buy something nice for yourself.

30
00:02:06,350 --> 00:02:09,880
Get that pizza or buy that book you always wanted.

31
00:02:09,890 --> 00:02:14,690
So make something nice for yourself for reaching the goal.

32
00:02:15,530 --> 00:02:21,380
Also, I will be adding new videos and resources to this course.

33
00:02:21,380 --> 00:02:23,270
So check this out.

34
00:02:23,540 --> 00:02:27,420
Check new information and continue improving yourself.

35
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:34,460
And also, if you have any questions or comments about this course, feel free to write me a message.

36
00:02:34,460 --> 00:02:39,410
I will be happy to communicate with you and address your comments.

37
00:02:40,180 --> 00:02:44,050
Thanks again and I wish you all the best.

38
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:45,440
By.
